# --- Generated junction mounts (naming convention: dot-prefix every one) ---
# All directory junctions this repo creates (vault link, agent-to-agent links,
# per-agent system/ mirror) are named with a leading "." specifically so this
# one block can ignore all of them by pattern. Agent-to-agent mounts in
# particular form a real cycle on disk (agents/repair/.agents/cleanup <->
# agents/cleanup/.agents/repair <-> ...); a reparse-point-unaware directory
# walk (git status, backup, indexers) recurses into that forever unless the
# mount dir itself is pruned before descent — which is what a gitignore'd
# directory name achieves. See Ensure-Junction / Ensure-AgentRelationLinks in
# agents/runtime/tools/setup-service.ps1 and its mirror in
# agents/repair/tools/repair_agent.py. Keep every new junction dot-prefixed
# and listed here — don't invent a differently-named mount.
.knowledge-base
.knowledge-base/
**/.knowledge-base/
knowledge-base/
**/knowledge-base/
.agents/
agents/*/.system/

